  "releaseNotes": "- Fixed: **words separated by an unusual space are two words.** A non-breaking space, the other\n        typographic spaces, a line break or a zero-width space between two words used to join them, so\n        \"DOUBLE CHOCOLATE\" written with a non-breaking space, or a name and a place on two lines, could\n        only be found as one long word. They now split words like an ordinary space. The invisible\n        characters that only join or mark text (the byte order mark, the word joiner and the zero-width\n        joiners) are removed.\n      - Fixed: **punctuation around a word no longer sticks to it.** Exclamation and question marks\n        (including the Spanish opening ones), double quotation marks and guillemets (« » ‹ ›), the\n        ellipsis character and the typographic hyphens now become a space, so \"hello!\" or a title in\n        quotation marks is found by its words. `#`, `@`, `%`, `=` and `+` are kept, since they are often part of what people search for.\n      - Changed: **ranking moves for text with these characters,** as the fixes above take effect. An\n        index picks this up at its next `Index()`, which the server runs whenever it loads a dataset.\n      - Changed: **a few engine classes are no longer public, and two methods are gone.** Code that used\n        `CoreSearchEngine`, `Document`, `CoreDocument`, `JsonParser`, `EmbeddingIndex`, `GetAllDocuments`\n        or `GetDocumentJsonOfKey` goes through `SearchEngine`: read a record with `GetJsonDataOfKey(long)`,\n        and a vector field through `SearchEngine.EmbeddingFields`.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IndxSearchLib",
